(6014812, 878879, 35560, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Magnum_za:</b></div><hr/><i> Water drops on flowers have been done to death. This however is beautifully done, and your exposure, lighting and composure as well as PP is top class. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I remember reading recently that we should not be criticizing photos because they use an idea that has "previously been done to death". Please remember there are those of us new to the forum and dp, and to whom these concepts are just delightful, and yes, even new.<br/> <br/>Also, each photo should be judged on its own merit.  Using your statement, should we exclude all the Icelandic Northern lights?<br/> <br/>I appreciate you did make some positive comments on this picture, but your "done to death" phrase really bothers me in this forum.</td>', 'Originally posted by Magnum_za: Water drops on flowers have been done to death. This however is beautifully done, and your exposure, lighting and composure as well as PP is top class.  I remember reading recently that we should not be criticizing photos because they use an idea that has "previously been done to death". Please remember there are those of us new to the forum and dp, and to whom these concepts are just delightful, and yes, even new. Also, each photo should be judged on its own merit.  Using your statement, should we exclude all the Icelandic Northern lights? I appreciate you did make some positive comments on this picture, but your "done to death" phrase really bothers me in this forum.', '2010-05-19 02:54:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6014813, 880175, 83785, '<td valign="top">Wow, this is a beautiful scene :-) love it :-) Also can''t believe I beat you in a challenge, hehe. That won''t happen often! lol<br/>Take care Nat, x</td>', 'Wow, this is a beautiful scene :-) love it :-) Also can''t believe I beat you in a challenge, hehe. That won''t happen often! lolTake care Nat, x', '2010-05-19 02:54:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6014819, 878879, 49109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by larushka:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Magnum_za:</b></div><hr/><i> Water drops on flowers have been done to death. This however is beautifully done, and your exposure, lighting and composure as well as PP is top class. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I remember reading recently that we should not be criticizing photos because they use an idea that has "previously been done to death". Please remember there are those of us new to the forum and dp, and to whom these concepts are just delightful, and yes, even new.<br/> <br/>Also, each photo should be judged on its own merit.  Using your statement, should we exclude all the Icelandic Northern lights?<br/> <br/>I appreciate you did make some positive comments on this picture, but your "done to death" phrase really bothers me in this forum. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>He is right, though, and as long as one is not voting an image lower therefor I see nothing wrong in such a statement.</td>', 'Originally posted by larushka: Originally posted by Magnum_za: Water drops on flowers have been done to death. This however is beautifully done, and your exposure, lighting and composure as well as PP is top class.  I remember reading recently that we should not be criticizing photos because they use an idea that has "previously been done to death". Please remember there are those of us new to the forum and dp, and to whom these concepts are just delightful, and yes, even new. Also, each photo should be judged on its own merit.  Using your statement, should we exclude all the Icelandic Northern lights? I appreciate you did make some positive comments on this picture, but your "done to death" phrase really bothers me in this forum.   He is right, though, and as long as one is not voting an image lower therefor I see nothing wrong in such a statement.', '2010-05-19 02:57:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6014820, 880132, 108580, '<td valign="top">"...and even a positive comment from Posthumous." pffffffft<br/>I nailed your Abstract feel, he didn''t! ;)</td>', '"...and even a positive comment from Posthumous." pffffffftI nailed your Abstract feel, he didn''t! ;)', '2010-05-19 02:57:53.000000', NULL, 0),
