(6016571, 878697, 69668, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LVicari:</b></div><hr/><i> njsabs? nicely lit! I am sure it is scoring well. THere was a time when I marveled at the eye processing here on this site, but now I have grown to dislike the obvious pimping. The whites are too white and the outlining of the pupil is too obvious. I have no problems with enhancing features, <b>just less is more..for me</b>.(maybe that''s why my portraits don''t score as well) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hello Leo....thanks for stopping by and making a comment.  Actually the only pimping on the eye is a color change.  She has more brown eyes than hazel.  No brightening of the whites and no outlining of the pupil.  I actually do not like over-pimping of portraits, especially in the skin.  I do appreciate the honestly in the comment.<br/> <br/>EDIT to add: I just saw your Azure entry from the April Freestudy.  Does she really have purple eyes? (sarcasm noted).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-05-21 13:11:32.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by LVicari: njsabs? nicely lit! I am sure it is scoring well. THere was a time when I marveled at the eye processing here on this site, but now I have grown to dislike the obvious pimping. The whites are too white and the outlining of the pupil is too obvious. I have no problems with enhancing features, just less is more..for me.(maybe that''s why my portraits don''t score as well)   Hello Leo....thanks for stopping by and making a comment.  Actually the only pimping on the eye is a color change.  She has more brown eyes than hazel.  No brightening of the whites and no outlining of the pupil.  I actually do not like over-pimping of portraits, especially in the skin.  I do appreciate the honestly in the comment. EDIT to add: I just saw your Azure entry from the April Freestudy.  Does she really have purple eyes? (sarcasm noted).', '2010-05-19 16:07:49.000000', '2010-05-21 14:11:32.000000', 0),
