(6017785, 880488, 96614, '<td valign="top">This is actually a REALLY great shot... i remember watching this on TV...  i''m quite surprised it didn''t do better!<br/> <br/>I might make a slight suggestion... to make the image "appear" sharper than it is you can "legally" cheat...  make a separate layer including just the background (do a VERY neat job of this) and do a VERY VERY tiny gaussian blur... just to make a slightly shallower DOF... EVER SO SLIGHTLY...  then re-size it with the long end at 1600 (twice the max) then sharpen the layer that shows the skaters... click on "filter" - "Sharpen" - "Sharpen"...  sharpen it twice... yea... too sharp... that''s good for now... then re-size it to 800 on the long end, and it won''t be too sharp any more... it will ne just right...<br/> <br/>just my two cents...  =)</td>', 'This is actually a REALLY great shot... i remember watching this on TV...  i''m quite surprised it didn''t do better! I might make a slight suggestion... to make the image "appear" sharper than it is you can "legally" cheat...  make a separate layer including just the background (do a VERY neat job of this) and do a VERY VERY tiny gaussian blur... just to make a slightly shallower DOF... EVER SO SLIGHTLY...  then re-size it with the long end at 1600 (twice the max) then sharpen the layer that shows the skaters... click on "filter" - "Sharpen" - "Sharpen"...  sharpen it twice... yea... too sharp... that''s good for now... then re-size it to 800 on the long end, and it won''t be too sharp any more... it will ne just right... just my two cents...  =)', '2010-05-20 00:55:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6017795, 880488, 96614, '<td valign="top">here''s a quick edit (hope you don''t mind)<br/> <br/>I added a motion blur to the background, sharpened the skaters, and did a curves adjustment to the skaters to make them stand out...<br/> <br/>the editing I did kinda sucks because I was only working with a screen shot of the image  =)    ... but you get the idea...<br/> <br/>.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=883788" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/95000-99999/96614/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_883788.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/95000-99999/96614/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_883788.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/95000-99999/96614/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_883788.jpg"/></a></td>', 'here''s a quick edit (hope you don''t mind) I added a motion blur to the background, sharpened the skaters, and did a curves adjustment to the skaters to make them stand out... the editing I did kinda sucks because I was only working with a screen shot of the image  =)    ... but you get the idea... .', '2010-05-20 01:08:08.000000', NULL, 0),
