(6073590, 878495, 75713, '<td valign="top">Excellent find! Finding a heron''s nest isn''t all that hard - what is hard is getting a shot of it as they usually build them so far up in a tree top you can''t get a shot. You did it!  Nice job getting detail under the wings too.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-06-30 13:15:54.</i></td>', 'Excellent find! Finding a heron''s nest isn''t all that hard - what is hard is getting a shot of it as they usually build them so far up in a tree top you can''t get a shot. You did it!  Nice job getting detail under the wings too.', '2010-06-30 00:44:27.000000', '2010-06-30 14:15:54.000000', 0),
(6074794, 880357, 91783, '<td valign="top">This is a WONDERFUL picture. I have always loved to look of this type of editing, but maybe bump up the contrast just a little? Maybe? just me... <br/> <br/>Would have given you a 8 or 9</td>', 'This is a WONDERFUL picture. I have always loved to look of this type of editing, but maybe bump up the contrast just a little? Maybe? just me...  Would have given you a 8 or 9', '2010-06-30 19:17:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6074945, 879528, 117831, '<td valign="top">I think this image had enormous potential. If you had done a longer exposure so that the water had a softer feel to it I think it would of been breathtaking. I love the colors in the sky, and I like the color and contrast of the buildings. The softer water would of made this image!</td>', 'I think this image had enormous potential. If you had done a longer exposure so that the water had a softer feel to it I think it would of been breathtaking. I love the colors in the sky, and I like the color and contrast of the buildings. The softer water would of made this image!', '2010-06-30 22:12:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6076432, 880336, 67697, '<td valign="top">Ok now based on our conversation, I''d say that this one is good with having your subject get the full attention.  The two things I think need changing are that the post is a little soft (I''m guessing this was a hand-held shot)and you have this cyan-green stuff in the trees.  This comes from playing with the saturation a bit too much.<br/> <br/>As a suggestion, for a lower light setting, and with using an Olympus:  You could actually go up to an ISO 400 and push for a little better shutter speed.  This helps steady those hand held shots.  Also, a lifesaver for all this noise that Oly puts out is to get Topaz Denoise 4.  My pics have never looked better.</td>', 'Ok now based on our conversation, I''d say that this one is good with having your subject get the full attention.  The two things I think need changing are that the post is a little soft (I''m guessing this was a hand-held shot)and you have this cyan-green stuff in the trees.  This comes from playing with the saturation a bit too much. As a suggestion, for a lower light setting, and with using an Olympus:  You could actually go up to an ISO 400 and push for a little better shutter speed.  This helps steady those hand held shots.  Also, a lifesaver for all this noise that Oly puts out is to get Topaz Denoise 4.  My pics have never looked better.', '2010-07-01 22:19:24.000000', NULL, 0),
